---
description: CycleSense CPH coding and research guardrails
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, and `docs/research_plan.md`.
Keep modeled cycling routes distinct from observed real bicycle trips.
Represent counters as eligible street segments; test detection through route–edge incidence.
Prefer a small reproducible pilot before large all-pairs or citywide computation.
Preserve training/evaluation scenario separation and random seeds.
Write unit tests for exact similarity, placement objectives, and new candidate/graph operations.
Never invent experimental findings or treat scenario-generated trip weights as measured flows.
